    "text": "To determine how much candy each person will have if they share it equally, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of candy.\n2. Divide the total amount of candy by the number of people.\n\nFirst, let's find the total amount of candy. Hugh has 8 pounds, Tommy has 6 pounds, and Melany has 7 pounds. So, the total amount of candy is:\n\\[ 8 + 6 + 7 = 21 \\text{ pounds} \\]\n\nNext, we need to divide the total amount of candy by the number of people. There are 3 people (Hugh, Tommy, and Melany). So, we divide 21 pounds by 3:\n\\[ 21 \\div 3 = 7 \\text{ pounds} \\]\n\nTherefore, if they share the candy equally, each person will have \\(\\boxed{7}\\) pounds.",
